{# Sponsor-level protocol section: no site, no subjects, no persons (D-005). Context: study, part #}
{% if part == "eligibility" %}
{{ section("5.1 Inclusion Criteria") }}
Participants are eligible for enrollment in protocol {{ protocol(study) }} only if all of the following apply:
1. Adults aged 18 years or older at screening with a confirmed diagnosis of {{ study.indication }}.
2. Adequate organ function as defined by the laboratory thresholds in Appendix 2.
3. Willing and able to comply with scheduled visits, treatment plan and laboratory tests.
4. Written informed consent obtained before any study-specific procedure.

{{ section("5.2 Exclusion Criteria") }}
1. Known hypersensitivity to {{ compound(study) }} or any of its excipients.
2. Estimated glomerular filtration rate below 45 mL/min/1.73 m2 at screening.
3. Participation in another interventional study within 30 days before the first dose.
4. Pregnancy or breastfeeding, or unwillingness to use highly effective contraception.
{% elif part == "statistics" %}
{{ section("9.4 Statistical Methods") }}
The primary analysis population for protocol {{ protocol(study) }} ({{ nct(study) }}; EudraCT {{ eudract(study) }}) is the full analysis set. Continuous endpoints are summarised with descriptive statistics and compared with an analysis of covariance adjusting for baseline value and stratification factors.
{{ section("9.5 Sample Size") }}
Assuming a two-sided significance level of 5% and a dropout rate of 10%, the planned sample size provides at least 85% power to detect the prespecified treatment difference.
{% else %}
{{ section("6.1 Study Treatment") }}
Investigational product {{ compound(study) }} is supplied as film-coated tablets for oral administration once daily with water. Dose modifications follow the toxicity management table in Section 6.4.
{{ section("6.2 Treatment Compliance") }}
Compliance is assessed at each scheduled visit by tablet count and review of the dosing diary.
{% endif %}
